description: "Free negative keyword generator for Google Ads. Pick from ready lists, add your own, choose a match type and check for conflicts with your keywords."
faqs:
  - q: "What are negative keywords in Google Ads?"
    a: "Negative keywords stop your ads from showing on searches that contain them. If you repair boilers and add jobs as a negative, your ads will not show for boiler engineer jobs. They are the main way to stop paying for clicks from people who were never going to buy."
  - q: "What is the difference between negative broad, phrase and exact match?"
    a: "Negative broad blocks a search if it contains all the negative words, in any order. Negative phrase blocks a search only if it contains the words in that exact order, with anything else around them. Negative exact blocks a search only if it is exactly that phrase with nothing added. Phrase match is the safest default for most lists."
  - q: "Do negative keywords block plurals and misspellings?"
    a: "No. Unlike normal keywords, negative keywords do not expand to close variants. Adding job will not block jobs, so add the singular, the plural and any common misspelling separately. The lists in this tool already include the usual pairs."
  - q: "Can negative keywords block searches I want?"
    a: "Yes, and that is the most common mistake. A negative of cheap blocks cheap plumber near me, which might be a perfectly good customer. Paste your keywords into the conflict checker in this tool and it flags any negative that would stop one of them from showing."
  - q: "Where should I add negative keywords?"
    a: "Use a shared negative keyword list for words that should be blocked everywhere, such as jobs and training, and apply it to every relevant campaign. Add campaign or ad group negatives for terms that only make sense in one place. Google Ads also supports account-level negatives for blocking terms across eligible campaigns."
  - q: "How often should I update my negative keyword list?"
    a: "Review the search terms report every week or two while a campaign is new, then monthly once it settles. The n-gram analyser on this site groups the report by repeated words, which makes new negatives much faster to find."
  - q: "Does this tool save my list?"
    a: "Yes, in this browser only, so your choices are still there next time on the same device. Nothing is uploaded or sent anywhere, including to me. The Reset button clears it."
