          <div class="tk-row">
            <button type="button" class="btn sm" id="kCopy">Copy list</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn ghost sm" id="kTxt">Download .txt</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn ghost sm" id="kCsv">Download CSV</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn ghost sm" id="kReset">Reset</button>
          </div>
          <p class="tk-hint">In Google Ads, open Tools, then Shared library, and find negative keyword lists (labelled Exclusion lists in newer versions). Create a list, paste this in, then apply it to your campaigns.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="fcard">
        <div class="fcard-head"><b>4. Conflict check</b><span>Protect your keywords</span></div>
        <div class="tk-body">
          <div class="field">
            <label for="kKw">Paste your keywords</label>
            <textarea id="kKw" class="tk-area" style="min-height:120px" placeholder="emergency plumber&#10;&quot;boiler repair near me&quot;&#10;[cheap plumber]" spellcheck="false"></textarea>
            <span class="tk-hint">Match type symbols are ignored. The check uses your chosen negative match type.</span>
          </div>
          <ul class="tk-list" id="kConf"></ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow pt0">
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Why every account needs a negative list</h2>
    <p>Google matches ads to searches more loosely every year. A keyword like boiler repair can show for boiler repair course, boiler engineer jobs and how to repair a boiler yourself. None of those people will hire you, and each click costs the same as a real customer. A good negative list is usually the fastest, cheapest improvement an account can make.</p>

    <h2>How to use these lists safely</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Read every word before you copy.</strong> A word that is waste for one business is a customer for another. Free is waste for most, yet free quote is a buying search for tradespeople, which is why it starts switched off.</li>
      <li><strong>Prefer phrase match.</strong> It blocks the words in order, which is precise without being as narrow as exact.</li>
      <li><strong>Run the conflict check.</strong> One careless negative can quietly switch off your best keyword.</li>
      <li><strong>Keep going after launch.</strong> Starter lists cover the predictable waste. Your own search terms report finds the rest, and the <a href="/tools/n-gram-analyser/">n-gram analyser</a> makes that quick.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Shared lists, campaign negatives and account negatives</h2>
    <p>Words that are wrong everywhere, such as jobs or training, belong in a shared list applied to every campaign. Words that are wrong only in one place belong on that campaign or ad group, for example blocking emergency on a planned-maintenance campaign so the emergency campaign gets those searches instead. If wasted spend keeps coming back however many negatives you add, the cause is usually match types or structure, which is what a <a href="/google-ads-audit/">$100 account analysis</a> looks at. Local businesses will find more on keeping spend inside the service area on the <a href="/google-ads-for-local-services/">local services page</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
(function(){
  'use strict';
  var $ = function(id){ return document.getElementById(id); };
  var KEY = 'df_negkw_v1';
  /* Each word: [text, on by default]. Off means it is often a buying search, so it is opt-in. */
  var GROUPS = [
    { id:'jobs', name:'Jobs and careers', on:true, words:[['job',1],['jobs',1],['career',1],['careers',1],['hiring',1],['vacancy',1],['vacancies',1],['salary',1],['salaries',1],['recruitment',1],['apprenticeship',1],['apprenticeships',1],['internship',1],['employment',1],['resume',1],['cv',1],['wage',1],['indeed',1],['glassdoor',1]] },
    { id:'learn', name:'Courses and training', on:true, words:[['course',1],['courses',1],['training',1],['certification',1],['certificate',1],['qualification',1],['degree',1],['diploma',1],['class',1],['classes',1],['college',1],['university',1],['school',1],['exam',1],['lesson',1],['lessons',1]] },
    { id:'diy', name:'DIY and how-to', on:true, words:[['diy',1],['how to',1],['yourself',1],['tutorial',1],['tutorials',1],['instructions',1],['manual',1],['step by step',1],['youtube',1],['video',0],['guide',0]] },
    { id:'research', name:'Research and definitions', on:true, words:[['what is',1],['meaning',1],['definition',1],['define',1],['wiki',1],['wikipedia',1],['example',1],['examples',1],['pdf',1],['history',1],['statistics',1],['template',1],['templates',1],['ideas',0]] },
    { id:'free', name:'Free and freebies', on:true, words:[['free',0],['freebie',1],['freebies',1],['giveaway',1],['torrent',1],['crack',1],['cracked',1],['download',0]] },
    { id:'used', name:'Second-hand', on:false, words:[['used',1],['second hand',1],['secondhand',1],['pre owned',1],['refurbished',1],['ebay',1],['gumtree',1],['craigslist',1],['marketplace',1]] },
    { id:'media', name:'Images and media', on:true, words:[['images',1],['image',1],['pictures',1],['picture',1],['photos',1],['png',1],['clipart',1],['wallpaper',1],['drawing',1],['coloring',1],['colouring',1],['logo',0]] },
    { id:'support', name:'Existing customers and support', on:false, words:[['login',1],['log in',1],['sign in',1],['my account',1],['customer service',1],['tracking',1],['cancel',1],['cancellation',1],['unsubscribe',1],['refund',1],['complaint',1],['complaints',1]] },
    { id:'trade', name:'Wholesale and trade', on:false, words:[['wholesale',1],['bulk',1],['supplier',1],['suppliers',1],['manufacturer',1],['manufacturers',1],['distributor',1],['trade price',1]] },
    { id:'price', name:'Low budget intent', on:false, words:[['cheap',1],['cheapest',1],['budget',0],['discount',0],['bargain',1]] }
  ];
  var state = { groups:{}, words:{}, match:'phrase' };

  function wkey(g, w){ return g + '|' + w; }
  function drawGroups(){
    $('kGroups').innerHTML = GROUPS.map(function(g){
      var on = state.groups[g.id];
      return '<div style="margin-bottom:18px">' +
        '<label class="tk-tog" style="font-weight:800"><input type="checkbox" data-group="' + g.id + '"' + (on ? ' checked' : '') + '><span>' + g.name + ' <span class="tk-hint" style="display:inline;font-weight:600">(' + g.words.length + ')</span></span></label>' +
        '<div class="tk-chips"' + (on ? '' : ' hidden') + '>' + g.words.map(function(w){
          var p = state.words[wkey(g.id, w[0])];
          return '<button type="button" class="tk-chip" data-g="' + g.id + '" data-w="' + w[0] + '" aria-pressed="' + (p ? 'true' : 'false') + '">' + w[0] + '</button>';
        }).join('') + '</div></div>';
    }).join('');
  }
  function lines(id){ return $(id).value.split(/\r?\n/).map(norm).filter(Boolean); }
  function norm(t){ return t.toLowerCase().replace(/^[\s"\[+-]+|[\s"\]]+$/g, '').replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim(); }

  function list(){
    var out = [], seen = {};
    GROUPS.forEach(function(g){
      if (!state.groups[g.id]) return;
      g.words.forEach(function(w){ if (state.words[wkey(g.id, w[0])] && !seen[w[0]]){ seen[w[0]] = 1; out.push(w[0]); } });
    });
    lines('kCustom').concat(lines('kLoc'), lines('kComp')).forEach(function(w){ if (!seen[w]){ seen[w] = 1; out.push(w); } });
    return out;
  }
  function wrap(w){ return state.match === 'phrase' ? '"' + w + '"' : state.match === 'exact' ? '[' + w + ']' : w; }

  /* does a negative block this keyword (treated as a search)? */
  function blocks(neg, kw){
    var nw = neg.split(' '), kws = kw.split(' ');
    if (state.match === 'exact') return neg === kw;
    if (state.match === 'broad') return nw.every(function(x){ return kws.indexOf(x) > -1; });
    return (' ' + kw + ' ').indexOf(' ' + neg + ' ') > -1;
  }

  function render(){
    var l = list();
    $('kCount').textContent = l.length;
    var out = $('kOut');
    out.textContent = l.length ? l.map(wrap).join('\n') : 'Switch on a group or add your own negatives.';
    out.classList.toggle('empty', !l.length);

    var kws = lines('kKw'), conf = [];
    kws.forEach(function(k){ l.forEach(function(n){ if (blocks(n, k)) conf.push([n, k]); }); });
    var c = $('kConf');
    if (!kws.length) c.innerHTML = '<li class="tk-chk mid"><i aria-hidden="true">!</i><span>Paste your keywords above to check them.</span></li>';
    else if (!conf.length) c.innerHTML = '<li class="tk-chk ok"><i aria-hidden="true">\u2713</i><span>No conflicts. None of these negatives blocks your ' + kws.length + ' keyword' + (kws.length > 1 ? 's' : '') + '.</span></li>';
    else c.innerHTML = conf.slice(0, 50).map(function(x){
      return '<li class="tk-chk no"><i aria-hidden="true">!</i><span><b>' + esc(wrap(x[0])) + '</b> blocks your keyword <b>' + esc(x[1]) + '</b></span></li>';
    }).join('') + (conf.length > 50 ? '<li class="tk-hint">and ' + (conf.length - 50) + ' more</li>' : '');
    save();
  }
  function esc(t){ return String(t).replace(/&/g,'&amp;').replace(/</g,'&lt;').replace(/>/g,'&gt;'); }

  $('kGroups').addEventListener('change', function(e){
    var g = e.target.dataset.group; if (!g) return;
    state.groups[g] = e.target.checked;
    e.target.closest('div').querySelector('.tk-chips').hidden = !e.target.checked;
    render();
  });
  $('kGroups').addEventListener('click', function(e){
    var b = e.target.closest('.tk-chip'); if (!b) return;
    var k = wkey(b.dataset.g, b.dataset.w);
    state.words[k] = !state.words[k];
    b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', state.words[k] ? 'true' : 'false');
    render();
  });
  [].slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('[data-m]')).forEach(function(b){
    b.addEventListener('click', function(){
      state.match = b.dataset.m;
      document.querySelectorAll('[data-m]').forEach(function(x){ x.classList.toggle('on', x === b); x.setAttribute('aria-pressed', x === b); });
      render();
    });
  });
  ['kCustom','kLoc','kComp','kKw'].forEach(function(id){ $(id).addEventListener('input', render); });

  function download(name, text, type){
    var a = document.createElement('a');
    a.href = URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([text], { type: type }));
    a.download = name; a.click(); setTimeout(function(){ URL.revokeObjectURL(a.href); }, 500);
  }
  $('kCopy').addEventListener('click', function(){
    var l = list(), b = this; if (!l.length || !navigator.clipboard) return;
    navigator.clipboard.writeText(l.map(wrap).join('\n')).then(function(){ var o = b.textContent; b.textContent = 'Copied'; setTimeout(function(){ b.textContent = o; }, 1400); });
  });
  $('kTxt').addEventListener('click', function(){ var l = list(); if (l.length) download('negative-keywords.txt', l.map(wrap).join('\n'), 'text/plain'); });
  $('kCsv').addEventListener('click', function(){
    var l = list(); if (!l.length) return;
    var mt = { phrase:'Phrase', exact:'Exact', broad:'Broad' }[state.match];
    download('negative-keywords.csv', 'Keyword,Match type\n' + l.map(function(w){ return '"' + w.replace(/"/g, '""') + '",' + mt; }).join('\n'), 'text/csv');
  });
  $('kReset').addEventListener('click', function(){
    try { localStorage.removeItem(KEY); } catch(e){}
    ['kCustom','kLoc','kComp','kKw'].forEach(function(id){ $(id).value = ''; });
    defaults(); drawGroups();
    document.querySelector('[data-m="phrase"]').click();
  });

  function defaults(){
    state.groups = {}; state.words = {}; state.match = 'phrase';
    GROUPS.forEach(function(g){ state.groups[g.id] = g.on; g.words.forEach(function(w){ state.words[wkey(g.id, w[0])] = !!w[1]; }); });
  }
  function save(){
    try { localStorage.setItem(KEY, JSON.stringify({ s: state, c: $('kCustom').value, l: $('kLoc').value, b: $('kComp').value, k: $('kKw').value })); } catch(e){}
  }
  function restore(){
    try {
      var d = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(KEY) || 'null'); if (!d || !d.s) return;
      Object.keys(d.s.groups || {}).forEach(function(k){ state.groups[k] = !!d.s.groups[k]; });
      Object.keys(d.s.words || {}).forEach(function(k){ if (k in state.words) state.words[k] = !!d.s.words[k]; });
      if (d.s.match) state.match = d.s.match;
      $('kCustom').value = d.c || ''; $('kLoc').value = d.l || ''; $('kComp').value = d.b || ''; $('kKw').value = d.k || '';
    } catch(e){}
  }

  defaults(); restore(); drawGroups();
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-m]').forEach(function(x){ var on = x.dataset.m === state.match; x.classList.toggle('on', on); x.setAttribute('aria-pressed', on); });
  render();
})();
</script>
